From: Nickolai Semendiaev <agent00791@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: skip uncreated links on scan failure

MLO links can exist before a vdev is created and assigned to a radio.
When a parallel scan fails, the cleanup loop also visits these links and
dereferences their NULL arvif->ar. Skip uncreated links, as the scan
cancellation path already does.

Signed-off-by: Nickolai Semendiaev <agent00791@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5806,7 +5806,7 @@ int ath12k_mac_op_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		links_map = ahvif->links_map;
 		for_each_set_bit(link_id, &links_map, ATH12K_NUM_MAX_LINKS) {
 			arvif = wiphy_dereference(hw->wiphy, ahvif->link[link_id]);
-			if (!arvif)
+			if (!arvif || !arvif->is_created)
 				continue;
 
 			ar = arvif->ar;
